# LOVE 11.5 colour/depth/MSAA capability probe
love version: 11.5.0 (Mysterious Mysteries)
renderer: OpenGL | 3.3.0 NVIDIA 591.86 | NVIDIA Corporation | NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650/PCIe/SSE2
canvas format depth16            supported=true
canvas format depth24            supported=true
canvas format depth32f           supported=true
canvas format depth24stencil8    supported=true
canvas format depth32fstencil8   supported=true
canvas format stencil8           supported=true
system limit canvasmsaa: 32

## 1. A depth attachment can be created and bound
newCanvas depth24stencil8 readable=true : ok=true
environment pass rendered -> capability-1-environment.png

## 2. The SAME depth attachment re-bound to a DIFFERENT colour target
actor pixels surviving the RETAINED depth test: 7980
partial-alpha pixels in that mask            : 0
NEGATIVE CONTROL, depth test off             : 14440
(the difference is the pillar's occlusion; equal counts would mean the
 retained depth attachment was NOT actually consulted)

## 3. Composite of environment colour + depth-tested actor
non-source-colour pixels in the composite: 0 / 61440

## 4. Post-processing the environment COLOUR leaves depth pristine
actor mask before vs after the colour post-process: 0 differing px

## 5. MSAA
requested msaa samples: 4
msaa colour canvas (msaa=4)                : ok=true 
msaa depth canvas, readable=true            : ok=false Readable depth/stencil Canvases with MSAA are not currently supported.
msaa depth canvas, readable unset           : ok=true 
bind msaa colour + msaa depth               : ok=true 
bind msaa colour + NON-msaa depth           : ok=false
MSAA environment: coverage-blended pixels = 888
actor pass against the MSAA depth attachment: ok=true
actor-mask pixels with PARTIAL alpha after resolve: 460
(non-zero => the pass-ownership boundary is coverage-blended,
 which is exactly what #836 forbids)

## 6. Is the depth attachment sampleable as a texture?
depthCanvas:setDepthSampleMode() : ok=true
sampling the depth canvas in a shader: ok=true 

## 7. Supersample-then-downsample as the alternative AA location
naive draw-at-1/3 with linear filter : blended pixels = 0
(zero => LOVE's linear filter is not a box filter; scaling down does
 NOT average the SS x SS block, so this is not supersampling at all)
explicit 3x3 box downsample        : blended pixels = 634
NOTE: that pass's depth attachment is 768x720, so it is NOT reusable as
the native-resolution actor depth without a second native-scale pass.

## 8. AA'd environment colour + native-resolution depth mask
actor-mask pixels with partial alpha: 0 (0 => genuinely binary)
environment colour still carries AA : 634 blended pixels
=> AA location and mask hardness are INDEPENDENT as long as AA lives
   in the colour path and the mask comes from a native-resolution
   depth attachment that no resolve ever touches.
